# Modes that change what the screen shows: DECTCEM, several modes in one sequence, unknown modes.

test DECTCEM hides and shows the cursor
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 2 5 l/h: DECTCEM
size 10 4
feed \e[?25l
cursor 1,1 hidden
feed \e[?25h
cursor 1,1 visible

test the cursor is shown at the start
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 2 5 h: show cursor (DECTCEM) is the default
size 10 4
feed x
cursor 1,2 visible

test hiding the cursor does not stop it moving
spec xterm ctlseqs DECTCEM: only the display of the cursor changes
size 10 4
feed \e[?25l\e[2;3H
cursor 2,3 hidden

test several modes can be set in one sequence
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? Pm h: Pm is a list
size 10 4
feed \e[?25l\e[?7;25h\e[?7;25l
cursor 1,1 hidden

test an unknown private mode changes nothing
convention modes a terminal does not know are ignored, the other modes in the sequence still apply
size 10 4
feed ab\e[?9999;25l\e[?9999h
cursor 1,3 hidden
screen
|ab|

test an unknown ANSI mode changes nothing
convention modes a terminal does not know are ignored
size 10 4
feed ab\e[999h\e[999l
screen
|ab|
cursor 1,3

test insert mode and new line mode can be set together
spec ECMA-48 8.3.125 SM / xterm ctlseqs CSI Pm h: Pm is a list
size 10 4
feed \e[4;20h\e[4$p\e[20$p
reply \e[4;1$y\e[20;1$y

test the modes of a screen are not shared with the alternate screen
convention insert mode is a terminal mode, not a screen property
size 10 4
feed \e[4h\e[?1049h\e[4$p
reply \e[4;1$y

test mode 5 reverse video can be asked for
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 5 h: reverse video (DECSCNM)
known-fail: alacritty – DECSCNM (mode 5) is not recognized: DECRQM answers 0
size 10 4
feed \e[?5$p\e[?5h\e[?5$p
reply \e[?5;2$y\e[?5;1$y

test mode 2 and mode 12 can be asked for
spec xterm ctlseqs CSI ? 1 2 h: start blinking cursor; CSI 1 2 h: send/receive
size 10 4
feed \e[12$p
reply~ \e[12;*$y

test the VT510 modes a terminal emulator has no hardware for are kept and answered
spec VT510 DECRQM and DECSET/DECRST: DECPFF 18, DECPEX 19, DECRLM 34, DECNRCM 42, DECKBUM 68, DECXRLM 73 and others are modifiable
known-fail: alacritty – these modes are not known: DECRQM answers 0
size 10 4
feed \e[?18$p\e[?18h\e[?18$p\e[?18l\e[?18$p
reply \e[?18;2$y\e[?18;1$y\e[?18;2$y
feed \e[?42$p\e[?42h\e[?42$p
reply \e[?42;2$y\e[?42;1$y
feed \e[?106h\e[?106$p\ec\e[?106$p
reply \e[?106;1$y\e[?106;2$y

test DECHCCM and the ECMA-48 modes without a terminal to apply to are permanently reset
spec VT510 DECRQM: DECHCCM (60), GATM, SRTM, VEM, HEM, PUM, FEAM, FETM, MATM, TTM, SATM, TSM and EBM are permanently reset
known-fail: alacritty – these modes are not known: DECRQM answers 0
size 10 4
feed \e[?60$p\e[1$p\e[5$p\e[19$p
reply \e[?60;4$y\e[1;4$y\e[5;4$y\e[19;4$y

test mode 41 makes a tab at the end of a row wrap first
convention xterm's ctlseqs "DECSET 41: more(1) fix"
known-fail: alacritty – these modes are not known: DECRQM answers 0
size 10 4
feed \e[?41$p\e[?41h\e[?41$p
reply \e[?41;2$y\e[?41;1$y
